  "summary": "NAR updates to BGC Atlas, PhageScope and MGnify, plus Unipept and NovoTax, extend scale and integration of microbial sequence and proteome annotation.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is large, curated resources that attach contextual annotation to microbial and phage sequence data. BGC Atlas v2 holds over 16 million predicted biosynthetic gene clusters searchable by taxonomic, environmental and geographic context. PhageScope 2.0 integrates genomic, functional and structural diversity at million-genome scale. MGnify v6 adds amplicon variant analysis, expanded viral and mobilome annotation, and Nextflow/Prefect automation. On the proteomics side, Unipept supports multi-sample metaproteomics comparison with confidence scoring and a faster API, while NovoTax builds sample-specific prokaryotic proteome databases from de novo MS data. Database-driven identification also appears in RADSuite (16S copy-number library, V-region detection for species-level calls) and metaEukaryome, which recovers eukaryotes from 75,727 metagenomes via organellar sequences. Outside this thread, a bacterial cis-eQTL study in E. coli and P. aeruginosa and the SNP2Cluster-Py transmission-clustering framework address pangenome regulation and pathogen epidemiology.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-opus-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-26"
}
